{"metadata":{"title":"Choosing a search tree","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a sorted set or sorted dictionary by the workload it will see."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sorted sets share one API: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetAlgebra"},{"text":"’s set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operations, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lowerBound(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"upperBound(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(in:)"},{"text":", and the elements as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank. Changing which one a program uses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a change of type name:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let avl: AVLTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let redBlack: RedBlackTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let bTree: BTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let skipList: SkipList = [40, 10, 30, 20]","","Array(avl)              \/\/ [10, 20, 30, 40], and the same for the others","avl.lowerBound(25)      \/\/ 2, the index of 30","bTree.lowerBound(25)    \/\/ 2"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one takes O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") per lookup, insertion and removal (expected for the treap and skip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list, amortized for the splay tree). They differ in the constant, in what else they offer, and in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which workloads they suit."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Lookups-and-scans-over-a-large-set-BTree","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Lookups and scans over a large set: BTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A B-tree node ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees"},{"type":"text","text":") holds tens of elements side by side, so a lookup reads a few nodes and few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cache lines, and iteration walks contiguous arrays. For a large set that is read far more often"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than it is changed, and for range scans, a "},{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the default. Copying a B-tree shares its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nodes, and a mutated copy copies only the nodes on the path it changes. "},{"code":"BTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its sorted dictionary."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Balanced-binary-trees-AVLTree-and-RedBlackTree","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Balanced binary trees: AVLTree and RedBlackTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"AVLTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps the heights of every vertex’s subtrees within one of each other, so it is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shallowest of the binary trees and the quickest of them to search. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"RedBlackTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" allows a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"taller tree and in return rotates at most two or three times per insertion or removal; prefer it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when changes outnumber lookups. Both convert to a Grafluent ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that shows the exact","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shape. ","type":"text"},{"code":"AVLDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the sorted dictionary in an AVL tree.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Splitting-and-joining-Treap","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Splitting and joining: Treap"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a random priority on each vertex, which makes its shape a random binary search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree’s whatever order the elements arrive in, and gives it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"split(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"join(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"join(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"OverlappingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the sets interleave. Pass a seeded generator to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Treap(_:using:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to make every shape reproducible. ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splits too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-working-set-of-hot-elements-SplayTree","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"A working set of hot elements: SplayTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"SplayTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps no balance information. ","type":"text"},{"code":"access(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and each mutation rotate the element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they reach to the root, so a run of lookups that keeps returning to a few elements finds them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"near the top:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Its other reads, ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" among them, leave the tree as it is, so they keep value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"semantics; use ","type":"text"},{"code":"access(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where the splay is wanted.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-sorted-queue-with-a-simple-structure-SkipList","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"A sorted queue with a simple structure: SkipList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A skip list (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists"},{"text":") stacks sorted linked levels, each holding about half the elements of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the one below. Its insertions touch only the levels an element reaches, and its levels are a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent graph through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"layersView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Keeping-every-version-PersistentTreeSet","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Keeping every version: PersistentTreeSet"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When old versions must stay readable, as in undo histories, snapshots handed to other tasks or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backtracking searches, a persistent set (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees"},{"text":") shares all but the vertices an edit touched:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let empty = PersistentTreeSet<Int>()","let one = empty.inserting(5)","let two = one.inserting(3)","let three = two.removing(5)","Array(one)                    \/\/ [5]","Array(two)                    \/\/ [3, 5]","Array(three)                  \/\/ [3]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each version costs O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") new vertices rather than a copy of the whole tree."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Summary","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Summary"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Workload"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Type"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Large sets, mostly lookups, range scans","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly lookups, a binary shape to inspect"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLTree"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLDictionary"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly insertions and removals"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"RedBlackTree","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splitting and joining sets"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Repeated access to a few elements"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SplayTree","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every version kept"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeSet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeDictionary"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A simple sorted queue"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SkipList","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/choosingasearchtree"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/persistenttrees":{"title":"PersistentTrees","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTrees"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","title":"GrafluentCollections","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph":{"role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/seeingacollectionasagraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Convert a collection’s shape to a Grafluent graph, then lay it out, write it or run an algorithm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","title":"Seeing a collection as a graph","kind":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Tries and suffix structures","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring."}]},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/RangeAndSpatialTrees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/rangeandspatialtrees","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Range and spatial trees","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Answer queries over ranges of a sequence, over intervals, and over points in space."}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/skiplists":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","title":"SkipLists","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkipLists"}]},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/DecisionDiagrams":{"role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/decisiondiagrams","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represent Boolean functions and families of sets as shared, canonical graphs."}],"title":"Decision diagrams","kind":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/btrees":{"title":"BTrees","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTrees"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees"}}}